    "text": "3 Inspiration\n\nTemple Run\n\nThe core gameplay was heavily inspired by the classic parkour game Temple Run. I extracted its mechanics of continuous running and extreme dodging, deeply integrating them with the rhythmic feel of keeping a dribble alive in basketball. Players must do more than just dodge; they need to constantly maintain ball control and make precise decisions on the move.\n\nShaolin Soccer\n\nWhen designing the obstacles, my main challenge was translating the intense defensive pressure of a basketball court into a single-player parkour experience. The movie Shaolin Soccer offered immense inspiration. I borrowed its surreal, exaggerated portrayal of sports, manifesting real-world \"dirty plays\" and invisible pressures as absurd physical obstacles. Players must evade sudden flying kicks from martial artists, foot-dragging slimes, and deadly floor spikes. This over-the-top approach significantly amplifies the kinetic tension and fun of the parkour while using dark humor to highlight the hardships the protagonist faces while chasing her dream."
