    "text": "Core Mechanics & Level Design\n\nThe core gameplay loop is built on a foundational logic of \"Cognition → Reaction → Overcoming.\" To ensure the parkour mechanics align perfectly with the narrative metaphor of an \"injury comeback,\" the game utilizes a design framework that alternates between situational tutorials and high-pressure combat.\n\nTutorial sequence, step 1: approaching the obstacle.\n\nTutorial sequence, step 2: the camera focuses on the training dummy and explains the action.\n\nTutorial sequence, step 3: returning to the running view.\n\nTutorial sequence, step 4: the player continues dribbling forward.\n\nThroughout the game, whenever a new obstacle makes its debut, the system triggers a dedicated tutorial phase: the action pauses instantly as the camera zooms in, using UI text to teach the dodge mechanics while revealing the physiological or psychological metaphor each trap represents in the player’s recovery journey. As players build their understanding of these metaphorical obstacles, the difficulty curve ramps up in a step-like manner. In the subsequent combat phases, dodge frequency spikes alongside a narrowing margin for error. This seamless shift from static learning to reflexive action creates an immersive simulation of the surging physical and mental pressure a player faces when moving from tedious rehab back into the heat of competition."
